"""Dish catalogue for the food-photo feature: what each recognised dish is
(region, category, veg/non-veg, description, main ingredients, food groups)
and its nutrition.

NUTRITION SOURCE — Indian Nutrient Databank (INDB), Vijayakumar et al.,
Current Developments in Nutrition 2024 (CC BY 4.0 article; data freely
available at github.com/lindsayjaacks/Indian-Nutrient-Databank-INDB-).
INDB computes recipe nutrition from ICMR-NIN Indian Food Composition Tables
(IFCT 2017) ingredient values. Numbers below are copied verbatim from
INDB.xlsx (per 100 g, rounded to 1 decimal) — generated by a script, not typed.

Reliability levels shown to users:
  high   — the same dish exists in INDB ("exact").
  medium — nearest INDB recipe used; the variant difference is explained ("closest").
  low    — no usable INDB recipe. Either the dish isn't in INDB, or INDB's
           value was excluded because it counts ALL deep-frying oil as eaten
           (a known limitation: 127 of INDB's 1,014 recipes exceed 40 g fat
           per 100 g). Values are the app's earlier rough per-serving
           estimates, labelled as such; fibre and sugar are left unknown.
           Burger has no value at all — none is shown rather than guessing.

Reference servings are typical single-person portions for display and
are fully adjustable by the user; they are not dietary prescriptions.
"""

